Expected Outcomes
After completing this lab, you should observe:

Performance Improvement: Materialized view queries should be 5-10x faster than base table queries
Storage Trade-off: Materialized views consume additional disk space
Data Freshness: Understanding the balance between query speed and data currency
Refresh Impact: Concurrent refresh allows queries during updates
Performance Benchmarks
Typical results on standard hardware:

Base table aggregation: 200-500ms
Materialized view query: 20-50ms
Refresh time: 1-3 seconds (depending on data volume)
Troubleshooting
Common Issues
Issue: Cannot create concurrent refresh

-- Solution: Ensure unique index exists
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_mv_unique ON mv_monthly_sales_summary(category, region, month);
Issue: Materialized view not updating

-- Check last refresh time
SELECT schemaname, matviewname, last_refresh 
FROM pg_stat_user_tables 
WHERE relname LIKE 'mv_%';
Issue: pg_cron extension not available

# Install from command line
sudo apt install postgresql-contrib
# Then in psql:
# CREATE EXTENSION pg_cron;
Issue: Slow refresh performance

-- Use CONCURRENTLY only when needed
-- For large updates, regular refresh is faster
REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW mv_monthly_sales_summary;
